<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  OWASP Dependency-Check suppressions for the cassyx reactor (plan section 11.1, `make cve-scan`).

  RULES FOR THIS FILE - read before adding anything:
  1. A suppression is only ever for a match that is WRONG (Dependency-Check pairs our jar with a
     CPE belonging to some other product). "Hard to upgrade" is not a reason; if a real finding
     cannot be fixed, leave the build red and escalate it.
  2. Every entry states the CVE, why it does not apply to us, and the evidence it was checked
     against - not "believed to be a false positive".
  3. No blanket <cve> without a <packageUrl>: a suppression must not silently cover a future
     dependency that really is affected.
-->
<suppressions xmlns="https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/dependency-suppression.1.3.xsd">

  <!--
    CVE-2023-37475 against org.apache.parquet:parquet-avro.

    Not applicable: the CVE is against hamba/avro, the GO implementation of the Avro codec
    (github.com/hamba/avro/v2). Its CPE is
      cpe:2.3:a:avro_project:avro:*:*:*:*:*:go:*:*
    - note the `go` target-software field - and the advisory's fix is a Go commit released as
    hamba/avro v2.13.0 (OSV GHSA-9x44-9pgq-cf45 / CVE-2023-37475; the affected range is a GIT range
    on https://github.com/hamba/avro). It has nothing to do with Apache Parquet or with the Java
    Apache Avro library.

    Dependency-Check matches it only because the artefact is called "*-avro" and the version number
    of the Parquet release happens to fall inside the Go package's "all versions before 2.13.0"
    range. Parquet's version line and Avro's are unrelated: parquet-avro 1.15.1 embeds Apache Avro
    (Java) 1.11.x, not "Avro 1.15.1", which has never existed.

    Evidence: OSV lookup of parquet-avro at 1.15.1, 1.15.2, 1.16.0, 1.17.1 and 1.18.0 reports
    CVE-2025-46762 (fixed by the upgrade to 1.18.0) and nothing else - CVE-2023-37475 is not
    associated with the Maven artefact at any version.

    Scoped to parquet-avro by packageUrl so that a genuinely affected dependency added later is
    still reported.
  -->
  <suppress>
    <notes><![CDATA[
      CVE-2023-37475 is a DoS in hamba/avro (Go). CPE target-software is `go`; the fix is
      hamba/avro v2.13.0. Not reachable from a Java Parquet dependency.
    ]]></notes>
    <packageUrl regex="true">^pkg:maven/org\.apache\.parquet/parquet-avro@.*$</packageUrl>
    <cve>CVE-2023-37475</cve>
  </suppress>

  <!--
    CVE-2026-66299 against org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core.

    Not applicable: the vulnerability is uncontrolled resource consumption in Tomcat's WebSocket
    CHAT EXAMPLE, which lives in the `examples` web application. NVD's own description says so
    outright, and adds: "Users who have followed the security guidance to remove the examples web
    application are not affected by this issue."

    The examples webapp ships only in the full Tomcat distribution (apache-tomcat-*.tar.gz). It is
    not in the embedded jar, which is the only Tomcat artefact cassyx ships. Verified by listing
    the jar: zero entries match `examples` or `chat`, and the only top-level packages are
    jakarta/servlet, jakarta/security and org/apache. There is no code path to the vulnerable
    component because the component is not present.

    This is a component-not-present suppression, NOT a risk acceptance. The version pin is already
    as high as it can go: every other Tomcat finding was cleared by moving to 10.1.57, and this one
    is fixed in 10.1.58, which Apache had not released to Maven Central at the time of writing.
    When 10.1.58 lands, raise <tomcat.version> and DELETE this entry rather than leaving it to rot.

    Scoped to tomcat-embed-core by packageUrl, so a full Tomcat distribution added later - which
    WOULD carry the examples webapp - is still reported.
  -->
  <suppress>
    <notes><![CDATA[
      CVE-2026-66299 is a DoS in Tomcat's WebSocket chat EXAMPLE. The examples webapp is not
      present in tomcat-embed-core (verified by jar listing), only in the full distribution.
      Fixed upstream in 10.1.58; remove this entry when that version is available.
    ]]></notes>
    <packageUrl regex="true">^pkg:maven/org\.apache\.tomcat\.embed/tomcat-embed-core@.*$</packageUrl>
    <cve>CVE-2026-66299</cve>
  </suppress>

</suppressions>
